<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narmer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3100 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narmer was an Egyptian king of around 3100 BCE, the last ruler of the Thinite line of Dynasty 0 and usually counted as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-babylonian-empire">First Dynasty</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmer-palette">Narmer Palette</a>, a carved ceremonial slate, shows him wearing the crowns of both Upper and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-egypt">Lower Egypt</a> and is often read as a record of the unification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. He is sometimes identified with the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menes">Menes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narmer.jpg" alt="Narmer" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narmer_palette_(obverse)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
